data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1506,"item_id":"fc_0360ee258724e882016adb503fc0188191b9b430a7c6bc4025","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R002\",\"packet_sha256\":\"2b472c05c89cef8952b2647cd47fd1fba7363692385881f72290703a858787da\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Packet-only mathematical review of R002. The first unsupported implication is in S002: from u(x,s)=q for x outside compact C, the argument asserts that the spatial complement of C is open and therefore the derivatives (including time and higher derivatives) vanish there. The packet has not established that C is closed before this use. M018 is listed, but its stated application is to K, not C; merely listing a theorem does not establish the needed fact. Thus smoothness and the H003 equality do not, as written, justify the asserted derivative vanishing or the resulting compact support/continuity properties used for the M001 integrability application and output. No repair is made here. Boundary: the supplied packet.json and declared Yui procedure only; no original source proof, other inference, previous audit, or external mathematical source was used. I make no runtime carrier or isolation attestation.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The stated direct input propositions and their stated bindings provide the premises used in the prose. In particular H003 supplies the exterior equality on J, and M001, M013, M014, M016, and M018 are explicitly available. Availability of M018 does not itself prove its unstated application to C.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"S001's boundedness-to-ball calculation is supported by M016 and elementary norm inequalities. The first material failure occurs in S002: the claim that the spatial complement of C is open, followed by derivative vanishing there, requires closedness of C. C is compact, but the prose does not apply M018 to C; its recorded application is to K. Consequently the smoothness/equality argument does not establish the claimed support properties and cannot establish the stated M001 hypotheses.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/4\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M001 and the volume/compactness results have identifiable intended roles. However the dependency accounting fails at S002's unproved assertion that the complement of C is open and the ensuing derivative vanishing. A theorem is available only through an actually justified application; the M018 entry binds it to K, not C. Those claims are essential to the asserted compact support and integrability.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/4\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The output is a detailed statement, but its claimed existence of J,C with all listed derivative and energy support properties, and its integrability conclusion, are not derived because of the S002 gap. Thus R002 does not establish the full output statement.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The proof fixes arbitrary t>0 and describes the resulting J and C within the inference; K is fixed arbitrarily for the compact-measure claim. The argument purports to conclude for arbitrary t. No witness escape or improper discharge is the first obstruction; mathematical adequacy is separately failed above.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The recorded bindings for the M inputs are generally identifiable. For M018, the actual application is to K, whereas the crucial assertion needs closedness of C. The listed application therefore does not verify that factual use. M001's compact-support hypothesis is also not established once the derivative-vanishing argument fails.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/4\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input statements and output statement spell out the relevant integrability, interval, compact-set, regularity, support, and measure claims sufficiently to assess this inference without consulting another proof body. This is a closure judgment, not a judgment that the output is proved.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/inputs/4/statement\",\"/inputs/5/statement\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The principal objects have declarations in the packet: parameters, D001/D004, statement binders, and local declarations for t,J,C,K,R₀,Q. However the actual prose also invokes closedBall, Euclidean topology/pseudometric, coordinate intervals, derivatives and measure notions whose declarations/precise semantics are not all inventoried as explicit packet objects or developed locally. This review does not treat the inventories as exhaustive proof of object closure.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/definitions\",\"/output/binders\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Actual factual uses include the claim that ℝⁿ's Euclidean/Borel setup has the required measure properties and, decisively, that C's complement is open so derivatives vanish outside C. No proved local fact or recorded M018 application supports the latter use. F001 only establishes boundedness of K in a ball and does not supply closedness of C.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/0/produces/0\",\"/inference/applications/4\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"I performed this mathematical review using the complete supplied packet.json and the declared Audit A, self-containment, and format guidance, with no other mathematical task material. From this packet alone R002 is insufficient for the stated output for the gap identified in S002. This records the review's input boundary and judgment, not a carrier identity, authenticated isolation, or runtime-attestation claim.\",\"locations\":[\"/packet_sha256\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/output/statement\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"substantive unsupported implication\",\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"premises\":\"H003 gives u(x,s)=q for x∉C and s∈J; C is declared compact; u is jointly smooth.\",\"conclusion\":\"The spatial complement of C is open, so derivatives (including the derivatives entering e_t) vanish outside C, yielding the stated continuity/support claims and the compact support needed for M001.\",\"basis\":\"The openness of the complement requires C to be closed. Although M018 is an allowed input stating compact sets are closed in Hausdorff spaces, the recorded application binds M018 to K, not C, and the prose does not establish C closed before making this inference. The unproved derivative/support claims invalidate the subsequent M001 application and block the output.\"}]}}"}

